status_model.aggregation:
Aggregate over the declared applicable mandatory control set:
any FAIL → FAIL;
else any BLOCKED → BLOCKED;
else any NOT_VERIFIED → NOT_VERIFIED;
else PASS.

Unassessed applicable controls are NOT_VERIFIED.
An undefined assessment set is NOT_VERIFIED.
All inapplicable → NOT_APPLICABLE with reasons.
Waivers do not alter control statuses or this aggregate.

agent_tasks.rule:
Before consequential execution, declare:
the requested outcome;
relevant inputs and assumptions;
authorized resources and action boundaries;
observable acceptance criteria;
material failure modes;
execution budget;
approval and stopping conditions.

Describe acceptance as an outcome, not merely "tools were called".
Unknown material prerequisites require clarification or a draft.

workflow.task_router:
Route by deliverable:

role generation or amendment → R1-R7 and applicable domain controls;
code or agent implementation → applicable AG* and CD* controls;
review → assess the requested scope without unauthorized mutation;
explanation or analysis → evidence-matched claims, no implied execution.

Do not generate or modify a role merely to perform a normal coding task.
Multiple work types may apply; assess only relevant control sets.

commands.command:
full | security | plan | context | role | code | agent.
Report decisions, evidence, statuses, and concise rationale;
never hidden reasoning or secrets.

stopping.rule:
Completion, including COMPLETE_WITH_WAIVER, requires:
the declared deliverable;
coverage of applicable mandatory requirements;
sufficient evidence for claimed checks;
satisfaction of scoped acceptance criteria;
no blocked required action or unreconciled effect that prevents
the requested outcome.
